This repository is licensed in two parts, because it holds two different kinds
of thing and one licence would be wrong for one of them.

CODE — the MIT Licence, below.
    Everything under `scripts/`, plus `config.example.env` and `requirements.txt`.

TEXT, FIGURES AND DERIVED DATA — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.
    Everything under `paper/`, `predictions/`, `prereg/`, `replication/`,
    `deposit/`, `figures/`, `docs/` and `spent/`, all top-level Markdown files,
    and the committed JSON result artifacts.

Attribution for the CC BY 4.0 part means citing the work as set out in
`CITATION.cff`.

NOT COVERED BY EITHER. The repository redistributes no third-party source. It
does hold data derived from public issue trackers and public git histories:

  * `.jira_*/` and `deposit/jira-caches-v1.tar.gz` are responses from the Apache
    Software Foundation's public Jira (https://issues.apache.org/jira). Apache
    Jira content is contributed under the Apache Contributor Licence Agreement
    and is redistributed here for reproducibility. Author display names appear in
    some records; `scripts/pseudonymize.py` is the tool provided for removing
    them.
  * `estimates_by_org.json` is derived from the Public Jira Dataset,
    Zenodo 15719919, which carries its own licence. Consult that deposit before
    redistributing anything derived from it.
  * `refminer_*.json` is the output of RefactoringMiner
    (https://github.com/tsantalis/RefactoringMiner), MIT-licensed, run over
    public Apache repositories. The output is data about those repositories, not
    a derivative of the tool.
  * `hadoop/`, `corpora/` and the probe clones are not committed. They are
    Apache Software Foundation repositories under the Apache Licence 2.0 and must
    be obtained from their own sources.

